\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 06 \'b7 Ship & Collaboration\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 We ran handoff as working sessions rather than a document: I walked the Raspberry team through the prototype flows for both classic and Boards on call, answered questions live, and left annotations where the prototype couldn't carry the detail. I'd built those prototypes in Claude Code, making a live walk through possible rather than a spec review.\
Asset: 06.png\
Everything shipped except the canvas notes. Engineers were still building Boards while adding guided workflows on a short timeline, so the notes were cut. They still aren't in the product as of writing, and I don't know if that's a decision or a backlog.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 07 \'b7 The Outcome\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Both tutorial systems are live. I asked Raspberry for usage after the fact. In the classic workspace, where the data exists, 1,168 designers viewed the workflows page over 90 days: 558 picked a workflow, 390 reached Generate, 382 generated, 204 downloaded \'97 17.5% end to end.\
The shape matters more than the total. Almost nobody who starts a workflow fails to finish, but half who reach the page never start one: the sequences hold, the entry point leaks.\
The caveats matter more than the figures: neither "viewed" nor "completed" is instrumented, so page views and downloads only stand in. Finishing a workflow isn't the same as understanding where Raspberry fits \'97 the actual objective \'97 and this is classic only; nothing equivalent exists for Boards.\
Whether this reduced onboarding calls is still unanswered. Call volume isn't in the analytics.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 08 \'b7 Reflection\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 I spent the design worrying about granularity: how finely to break each workflow into steps. I settled it by argument, with no data.\
The numbers indicate I was worrying about the wrong half. The loss is at the entry point, which I designed as a way in, not as a persuasion. I never asked which part was most likely to fail, and the answer was the part I'd thought about least.\
}